    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65/9af2a4f1-6b52-480b-a69f-d59b265be598/16",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65/9af2a4f1-6b52-480b-a69f-d59b265be598/24",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65/9af2a4f1-6b52-480b-a69f-d59b265be598/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65/9af2a4f1-6b52-480b-a69f-d59b265be598/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Esmé Cowles",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8aeffacfd6007656bf65",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a519bb0b0500707c7173\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a519bb0b0500707c7173\" data-account-id=\"6089a519bb0b0500707c7173\" accountid=\"6089a519bb0b0500707c7173\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Adam Wead</a>, yes, I think that's the way to go.  You might want to add some children of a resource with hasMember links to have both ldp:contains and pcdm:hasMember on the same resource.  Then you can set --predicate to <a href=\"http://pcdm.org/models#hasMember\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://pcdm.org/models#hasMember</a> and it should export the members, but not things that are directly contained.  Setting it to <a href=\"http://pcdm.org/models#hasMember,http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#contains\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://pcdm.org/models#hasMember,http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#contains</a> should export both.</p>",
     "created": "09/Dec/16 10:38 AM",
